  "published": "2026-08-01T11:29:23.017Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "PLACEMENT: automatic placement now EXECUTES its partial-GPU plan. A model too large for VRAM but fitting host RAM previously logged \"k of N layers stay on the GPU\" and then attempted a whole-model device move — a guaranteed CUDA OOM on exactly the hardware the plan had just measured. It now loads as pinned-prefix streaming: the first k blocks stay resident in VRAM and the tail pages through one rolling slot fed from the (page-cached) checkpoint. MEMORY: NVMe-paged optimizer state is rehydrated correctly — the async prefetch promoted moments into an internal cache while the optimizer kept reading 0-element placeholders from its state dict, so any over-RAM-budget run either crashed on a shape mismatch or silently lost Adam moments; restored tensors are now swapped back into the state dict. Model merging is memory-bounded as intended: every tensor materialized for a parameter (reader outputs, deltas, reduce partials) dies with a per-parameter dispose scope, only the merged result survives, and readers plus Fisher maps are released on every exit path including early errors — a leaked reader also pinned checkpoint files against deletion on Windows. SERVING: tool_choice \"required\"/named now works together with an assistant prefill — the forced call is parsed from the generated text alone (prose in front of the JSON made the strict parse fail, silently downgrading every prefilled forced-tool request to a \"stop\" response carrying raw JSON), streaming no longer duplicates the prefill chunk in the fallback, and the withheld-text fallback now passes through the output guardrails instead of bypassing them. fuuga-serve warns at startup that --offload is not supported for generation (previously it failed on the first token with a bare cross-device error). A2A: the agent card is also served at /.well-known/agent-card.json, the v1 spec path SDK resolvers fetch. DEPENDENCIES: ModelContextProtocol 2.0.0, A2A SDK 1.0.0-preview2 (client rewritten to the v1 flat-Part/oneof API), Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime 1.28.0, Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.8.3, OpenTelemetry 1.17.0, Serilog 4.4.0, and other minor updates. SIZING: training-state estimates now match measured behavior (8 bytes/param in bf16 — moments follow the parameter dtype and there are no fp32 master weights), so config derivation stops overstating memory 2.25x and pushing NVMe paging onto models whose state fits in RAM. VISION: new `train-vision` and `caption` commands make a Fuuga LM caption images natively, with no external captioner. `train-vision` runs the LLaVA-style two-stage protocol over a directory of images plus a captions.tsv manifest: stage 1 aligns a vision projection against a frozen CLIP ViT-L/14 encoder (initialize with --clip <safetensors>) and frozen LM — cheap enough for a 6 GB GPU — and stage 2 unfreezes the LM; optional --augment applies label-preserving shift/flip jitter. `caption` decodes the image (SkiaSharp, new dependency), feeds projected CLIP features through a new embeddings-based cached prefill (forwardCachedFromEmbeddings — image features have no token IDs to look up), and decodes through the ordinary KV-cached loop with greedy or temperature sampling; the checkpoint directory is self-describing (vision.json sidecar + copied LM metadata). The embeddings prefill path is parity-tested bit-identical against the token path.",
